[Event "Ruy Lopez"]
[Orientation "white"]
[Pitch "The Spanish: pressure on the knight that guards e5, and a slow fight for the centre."]

1. e4 { Take the centre and open lines for your queen and bishop. } 1... e5
2. Nf3 { Develop with a threat: the knight attacks e5. } 2... Nc6
3. Bb5 { Pressure the knight that defends e5. } 3... a6
( 3... Nf6 4. d3 { Against the Berlin, keep it simple: protect e4 and develop. } 4... Bc5
5. c3 { Prepare d4 and give the bishop a retreat square. } 5... O-O
6. O-O { King safe; the position is quiet and easy to play. } 6... d6
7. h3 { Keep the bishop out of g4. } )
( 3... d6 4. d4 { Against the Steinitz, open the centre while Black is cramped. } 4... Bd7
5. Nc3 { Develop and add pressure on e5. } 5... Nf6
6. O-O { Castle before the centre opens. } 6... Be7
7. Re1 { Defend e4 so the knight on c3 is free to move. } )
( 3... Bc5 4. c3 { Prepare d4, which will hit the bishop on c5. } 4... Nf6
5. d3 { Protect e4 first; d4 can come later. } 5... O-O
6. O-O { Castle; this transposes to the quiet lines. } 6... d6 )
4. Ba4 { Keep the pin; taking on c6 gives up the bishop pair for nothing yet. } 4... Nf6
5. O-O { Castle: e4 is safe because Re1 is coming. } 5... Be7
6. Re1 { Protect e4 for good. } 6... b5
7. Bb3 { The bishop retreats but still aims at f7. } 7... d6
8. c3 { Prepare d4 and keep a home for the bishop on c2. } 8... O-O
9. h3 { Stop ...Bg4 before you play d4. } *
